1
00:04:35,454 --> 00:04:41,454
Start your engines...

2
00:09:10,909 --> 00:09:16,909
Herbie Fully Loaded is a comedy, family, adventure
film directed by Angela Robinson.

3
00:13:46,363 --> 00:13:52,363
Maggie Peyton, the new owner of Number 53 - the free-wheelin' Volkswagen bug with a mind of its
own - puts the car through its paces on the road to becoming a NASCAR competitor.

4
00:18:21,818 --> 00:18:27,818
Maggie Peyton, played by Lindsay Lohan.

5
00:22:57,272 --> 00:23:03,272
Ray Peyton Sr., played by Michael Keaton.

6
00:27:32,727 --> 00:27:38,727
Trip Murphy, played by Matt Dillon.

7
00:32:08,181 --> 00:32:14,181
Ray Peyton Jr., played by Breckin Meyer.

8
00:36:43,636 --> 00:36:49,636
Kevin, played by Justin Long.

9
00:41:19,090 --> 00:41:25,090
Sally, played by Cheryl Hines.

10
00:45:54,545 --> 00:46:00,545
Herbie: Fully Loaded is a 2005 American sports comedy film directed by Angela Robinson from a
screenplay written by Thomas Lennon, Robert Ben Garant, Alfred Gough, and Miles Millar.

11
00:50:30,000 --> 00:50:36,000
The film stars Lindsay Lohan as the youngest member of an automobile-racing family, Michael Keaton as her father,
Breckin Meyer as her brother, Justin Long as her romantic interest, and Matt Dillon as a competing racer.

12
00:55:05,454 --> 00:55:11,454
Herbie: Fully Loaded features cameo appearances by many NASCAR drivers,
including Jeff Gordon, Jimmie Johnson, Tony Stewart, and Dale Jarrett.

13
00:59:40,909 --> 00:59:46,909
Produced by Robert Simonds, Herbie: Fully Loaded is the sixth and final installment in the Herbie film series, following the
television film The Love Bug (1997), and the first theatrical feature film since Herbie Goes Bananas (1980).

14
01:04:16,363 --> 01:04:22,363
It serves as a legacy sequel to the previous films.

15
01:08:51,818 --> 01:08:57,818
Principal photography took place from August to November 2004, with cinematographer Greg Gardiner, at various locations in California, including
the Riverside International Raceway and Auto Club Speedway; Hansen Dam in Los Angeles; and at Walt Disney Studios in Burbank.

16
01:13:27,272 --> 01:13:33,272
During post-production, editing was completed by Wendy Greene
Bricmont, and the score was composed by Mark Mothersbaugh.

17
01:18:02,727 --> 01:18:08,727
The film premiered at the Las Vegas Motor Speedway on May 10, 2005, and Walt Disney
Pictures released it theatrically in the United States on June 24.

18
01:22:38,181 --> 01:22:44,181
Distributed by Buena Vista Pictures Distribution, Herbie: Fully Loaded was a box office success,
grossing over $144 million worldwide against its production budget of $50 million.

19
01:27:13,636 --> 01:27:19,636
The film received mixed reviews from critics and moviegoers, but a
positive response from fans of the Herbie franchise.

20
01:31:49,090 --> 01:31:55,090
The film explores themes of car race, sports, victory, sequel, slapstick comedy.

21
01:36:24,545 --> 01:36:30,545
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
